{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared HMAC test vectors for the core<->search internal contract.",
    "Owned by vizra-core; vizra-search vendors a byte-identical copy and tests",
    "against it. If the two repositories disagree here they would sign",
    "different bytes and every internal call would 401 in production.",
    "Scheme: api/search-internal.openapi.yaml, components.securitySchemes.hmacSignature.",
    "canonical_string joins six fields with a single \\n and has no trailing newline.",
    "Generated independently of the Go implementation (python hmac/sha256).",
    "",
    "`vectors` are ACCEPT cases. `negative_vectors` are REJECT cases, and they",
    "matter more: agreeing on what is accepted while disagreeing on what is",
    "rejected is how two implementations of the same scheme diverge. Every",
    "negative vector carries a GENUINE signature over exactly the fields as",
    "sent, so only the stated rule can refuse it — a vector whose signature was",
    "simply wrong would prove nothing.",
    "Negative vectors are judged against `verifier_now_unix` as the verifier's",
    "clock."
  ],
  "scheme": "v1",
  "key_utf8": "Ar4Lo8Cq2Ei6Uk0Wn3Sv7Yb1Md5Pt9Xz",
  "key_utf8_warning": "TEST VECTOR ONLY. This value is published in a public repository and must NEVER be used as SEARCH_HMAC_KEY, VIZRA_SESSION_SECRET or any other configuration value. vizra-core's production loader refuses it by exact match (knownPublishedSecrets in internal/config/config.go); vizra-search must do the same. Generate a real key with `openssl rand -base64 32`.",
  "max_clock_skew_seconds": 300,
